To minimize the JudyHS overhead, would could index this:

```c
struct label_registry_idx {
   STRING *key;
   STRING *value;
};
```

So, instead of indexing `key:value` we could always index 16 bytes with the pointers.

We could also use a JudyL on `STRING *key`, and each entry to have a JudyL on `STRING *value`.

This will greatly improve performance too.
